I go to the reception desk.
There is a young man there.
I say to him, "Hello, Dada, I want to play here today."
"I am new here."
"I am a guest today."
He says, "No problem, madam."
"Do you know how to play badminton?" he asks.
I smile and say, "Yes, I do."
"How much is the fee for one day?" I ask.
He says, "Two hundred rupees, madam."
I give him two hundred rupees.
I do not have my own racket in Mumbai.
I ask, "Can I get a racket on rent?"
He gives me a blue racket.
He says, "The rent for the racket is fifty rupees."
I pay fifty rupees for the rent.
I take the racket in my hand.
I check its weight.
It is light and nice.
I thank him and go to play.
